  "title": "Schanuel's Conjecture",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Conjecture Given any $n$ complex numbers $z_1,...,z_n$ which are linearly independent over the rational numbers $\\mathbb{Q}$, then the extension field $\\mathbb{Q}(z_1,...,z_n,\\exp(z_1),...,\\exp(z_n))$ has transcendence degree of at least $n$ over $\\mathbb{Q}$.",
